# Rust backend

- Chess rules and legal moves: Shakmaty only.
- Keep Tauri commands thin: parse input, call `game` / `engine`, return serializable DTOs.
- Keep engine integration in `engine/` — isolated from UI and from `game` rules logic.
- MVP: no network, no filesystem engine install, no real UCI process management.
- Add crates with `cargo add` from `src-tauri`, not hand-edited `Cargo.toml` dependency lines when CLI works.
